---
import SocialIcons from '#components/SocialIcons/SocialIcons.astro';
import './CV.css';
---

<div class="cv">
  <h2 class="title section">
    Janis Jansen
    <span class="raw-only">
      <a href="mailto:mail@janis.me">mail@janis.me</a>
      <SocialIcons />
    </span>
  </h2>
  <p class="subtitle section">Typescript ■ React ■ SCSS ■ Python ■ SQL ■ Three.js ■ Go ■ WASM ■ Vue ■ Solid</p>
  <div class="intro section">
    <div class="body">
      <p>
        Hi, I'm Janis, a 25-year-old full-stack engineer from Germany. I'm working on complex, modern web applications
        across the entire stack, from database to (mostly?) pixel-perfect UI. With my experience in building
        interactive, data-intensive applications in various industries, I am very excited to develop the next
        cutting-edge product (with you?).
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="education section">
    <h3>Education / Skills</h3>
    <div class="body">
      <p>
        I have been working full-time in software development for the last 9 years, gaining a lot of experience in
        various fields. A rough, ranked list of expertise:
      </p>

      <ol start="0">
        <li><b>Typescript</b>: Expert</li>
        <li><b>CSS</b>/<b>SCSS</b>: Very Advanced</li>
        <li><b>Vite</b>: Very Advanced</li>
        <li><b>React</b>: Advanced</li>
        <li><b>WebAPIs</b>: Advanced</li>
        <li><b>Three</b>.js: Experienced</li>
        <li><b>Python</b>: Experienced</li>
        <li><b>Docker</b>: Experienced</li>
        <li><b>Postgres</b>: Proficient</li>
        <li><b>Rust</b>: Proficient</li>
      </ol>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Courses</b></li>
        <ul>
          <li>Advanced 3D Rendering in OpenGL/WebGL and Vulcan (2023)</li>
        </ul>
        <ul>
          <li>Deep-dive into Vite internals (Live-course @ViteConf 2024)</li>
        </ul>
      </ul>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Seminars</b></li>
        <ul>
          <li>Data safety and compliance: Done every year since 2022 :(</li>
          <li>preparation seminar for TISAX and ISO 27001 in 2024</li>
        </ul>
      </ul>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Apprenticeship</b></li>
        <ul>
          <li>IT specialist for application development</li>
          <li>2016-2019</li>
        </ul>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="experience section">
    <h3>Work-experience</h3>
    <div class="body">
      <ul>
        <li>
          <b>Cognigy</b>: Sr. Software Engineer (Jul 2025 - present)
          <ul>
            <li>
              Working on Cognigy's low-code conversational AI platform, mainly on the frontend for the conversation
              simulation feature (Test AI Agent flows with LLM-powered simulations). Also working on customer metric
              dashboards, insights/analytics, live streaming of chat conversations and more.
            </li>
            <li><b>Stack</b>: Typescript, React, CSS, Redux, Styled components, Node</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>Dive CAE</b>: Sr. Fullstack developer (Oct 2021 - Jun 2025)
          <ul>
            <li>
              Built a cloud-native CAE simulation platform including streaming and visualization of <b
                >simulation results</b
              >, data analysis tools, user management, Python SDKs and more. Leading the frontend development team to
              develop an industry-leading 3D interface for the best-in-class cloud-native CAE application.
            </li>
            <li>
              <b>Stack</b>: Typescript, React, Threejs, Go, WebAssembly, Zustand, SCSS, FastAPI, Comlink, SQLAlchemy,
              Postgres, Temporal
            </li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>SMS Digital</b>: Fullstack developer (Jul 2020 - Sep 2021)
          <ul>
            <li>
              Worked on multiple solutions within the predictive quality division. All apps deal with predicting and
              optimizing properties and factors in the areas of steelmaking. Built live dashboards, Human-machine
              interfaces, statistical models, data-streaming APIs and more.
            </li>
            <li><b>Stack</b>: React, Less, FastAPI, SQLAlchemy, SciPy, Tensorflow, D3js, Plotly</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>SMS Group</b>: Software engineer (Sep 2016 - Jul 2020)
          <ul>
            <li>
              Modernizing SMS's R&D department by migrating physical and mathematical models to the web, building new
              web applications for interacting with simulation data and for visualizing results in 3D.
            </li>
            <li><b>Stack</b>: Angular, Less, C++, Fortran, Python</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="random section">
